From 28d3b400fdcd3204a9cf200aef07f30b272a5d5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:39:21 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): add /video chat command for literal
 text-to-video
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Type "/video <description>" in the main chat to generate a short clip:
renders frame 0 with txt2img, chains subsequent frames through img2img
at a low denoising strength for smooth motion, then stitches to mp4
with ffmpeg. Shares Forge/VRAM plumbing with image generation.

Deliberately literal, same contract as the existing /generate raw-image
endpoint: unlike /image, it never pulls scene details from the roleplay
conversation via image/prompt.py's action-detection/appearance
injection — only the text typed after /video is used.

- server/image/video.py: frame-chain generation + ffmpeg stitching
- server/config.py: video config block (frames, fps, steps, denoise)
- server/routes/image_api.py: /video-generate, /video-progress, /video-interrupt
- server/static/app.js: /video command, triggerVideo(), video-aware history strip
- server/static/style.css: video thumbnail sizing in the history strip
